{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1495385-episode-and-story-ideas-for-vampire-the-masquerade","id":1495385,"title":"Episode and story ideas for Vampire: The Masquerade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-21T16:11:27-07:00","id":1495385,"title":"Episode and story ideas for Vampire: The Masquerade","content":"<b>You Give:</b> Plot ideas! Hopefully better fit for a standalone story or episodic chapter rather than long-form chronicle pitches (i.e., the plot thread should be able to be wrapped up in no more than a few sessions). Assumptions may vary but I generally come up with ideas presuming Modern Nights (at or near Current Year) chronicles for a Coterie of 4-6 Neonate Vampires, who will be all or mostly of the Core/&quot;Pillar&quot; Clans and Camarilla or Anarch by sect.<br /> <br /> <b>I Offer:</b> The first few to get us started!<br /> <br /> 1. A prominent member of the local Blood Doll scene, and a favorite &quot;feeding partner&quot; of several Kindred, has been embraced. Now he's showing up at his old haunts and bragging about &quot;becoming a real vampire.&quot; Minor Masquerade-Breach aside, it is not unlikely at least some of this scenester's Kindred patrons will want to adopt the Caitiff. The Coterie might wish to take him aboard themselves, ransom him off to one of his undead <i>paramours</i>, or simply try to find out who performed the illegal embrace.<br /> <br /> 2. A Malkavian tired of the lies and politesse that keep Kindred society running has created a designer party drug which all the cool kids are dying to try. With the cocktail in their systems, the blood of the unwitting kine becomes psychoactive and gives the Kindred who feed on them revelatory but paranoia-inducing visions. After just one &quot;trip,&quot; Kindred either begin to see plots where there are none, or refuse to conceal loathing for their fellows. In subsequent nights, simmering feuds between Kindred explode into open conflict all over the city, creating chaos.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3. A local Kindred of Prominence announces that he is leaving the city and cutting all ties. He happens to own the deed on a relatively new and very ritzy mixed-use building in the heart of the city: shops and bars below, condominiums above. There's even a rooftop swimming pool, frequently the scene of late-night private parties. It's ideal as Domain and feeding ground, and it shall go to the Kindred or group of Kindred who can make the most enticing offer. Cash is good, but the owner is willing to entertain all sorts of offers for the building.<br /> <br /> 4. A rising internet star trying to make a splash as a &quot;ghost hunter&quot; accidentally exposes an isolated and semi-feral Kindred to sunlight while exploring the apparently abandoned country house that served as the vampire's lair. Digital video of the Kindred frenzying, hitting one person hard enough to put them in traction, and burning to charred bones in seconds is immediately uploaded to the influencer's channel. There's no scrubbing the video now, and the elders want some young kindred opinions on how to handle the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","user":"Ventrue Busboy","date":". 10-21-2022, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T19:02:52-07:00","id":1495399,"title":"","content":"A few ideas for shorter games...<br /> <br /> 1. All assamite coterie, each character is a specialist in a different mode of death; sniper, poisons, melee combat, explosives, spray and pray guns, etc. Each session starts with a breakdown of the target, the local complications, optional objectives, and the like. The group plans the work and then works the plan. Yes, this is just a vampiric TTRPG variant of the Hitman video game series, but it makes things very self-contained and allow for a lot of variety in locations and stories.<br /> <br /> 2. A group of Nosferatu and a group of Tzimisce are fighting over the sewers in a contested city. The Nosferatu have their spawning pools and mutated critters, while the Tzimisces have their modified ghouls. Whoever creates the best battle plans wins the city underground. The players can be either side in the conflict based on tastes.<br /> <br /> 3. The Giovanni Endless Night plan has come to pass, but it didn't quite work how they thought it would. The dead rise as flesh eating zombies that attack the living, but mostly ignore vampires unless attacked. Congratulations, every vampire coterie is now scrambling to round up humans into &quot;safe zones&quot; to preserve their only food supply. Needless to say, the masquerade is no longer a concern, but the mind set change to go from hunting humans to protecting them, if only as cattle, is quite the core game whiplash. This gets even more interesting when you have to figure out how to control things during the daylight hours.<br /> <br /> 4. The coterie is a group of CEO types who pool their various expertise and power to create a power block in their country. This is specifically designed to function beyond a local city style of game because the focus will be on Backgrounds, rather than disciplines or clan/faction membership. This will feel more like a vampire themed 4X strategy game than a TTRPG session. If that is too abstract, keep the PC vampires making the Background related moves, while during the action phases the PCs play the ghouls of those CEOs who have to make the acquisitions and political influence happen.<br /> <br /> 5. The Tremere have a rogue on their hands. The only problem is that they can't quite seem to kill him on their own. The rogue uses Path of Conjuring to create living duplicates of himself or finely tuned combat bodies, then uses Dominate to possess them. Path of Conjuring also allows for things like explosives, bomb vests and dead man's switches to be created. How do you kill someone who could look like anyone, probably kill you when they die, but then keep coming back? Add in a high auspex rank to do some astral scouting and this is quite the difficult character to lock down in any way. Basically, it is a vampire version of Altered Carbon, except the PCs don't get to needle cast out of their bodies if things go wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T04:42:05-07:00","id":1495416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1495385-episode-and-story-ideas-for-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1495399#post1495399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few ideas for shorter games...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 4. The coterie is a group of CEO types who pool their various expertise and power to create a power block in their country. This is specifically designed to function beyond a local city style of game because the focus will be on Backgrounds, rather than disciplines or clan/faction membership. This will feel more like a vampire themed 4X strategy game than a TTRPG session. If that is too abstract, keep the PC vampires making the Background related moves, while during the action phases the PCs play the ghouls of those CEOs who have to make the acquisitions and political influence happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have homebrewed a system to use backgrounds in a more meaningful/strategical way. My chronicle is more traditional, but one of the Characters is a powerful arms industry tycoon and he can engage in economical warfare against his rivals. Apart for that, all Backgrounds have an in-game use, as they have to be &quot;tapped&quot; to get info, special equipment or favours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T05:05:17-07:00","id":1495420,"title":"","content":"'A prominent member of the local Blood Doll scene, and a favorite &quot;feeding partner&quot; of several Kindred, has been embraced. Now he's showing up at his old haunts and bragging about &quot;becoming a real vampire.&quot; Minor Masquerade-Breach aside, it is not unlikely at least some of this scenester's Kindred patrons will want to adopt the Caitiff. The Coterie might wish to take him aboard themselves, ransom him off to one of his undead <i>paramours</i>, or simply try to find out who performed the illegal embrace'<br /> <br /> why has the caitff not met final death yet?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T08:15:22-07:00","id":1495431,"title":"","content":"The Prince has disappeared (and several signs point to possibly destroyed). The Sheriff and Seneschal each suspect the other of being responsible but can't prove it. Each side is currently gathering potential allies for what looks to be an inevitable conflict. Other forces are also looking for ways to turn this to their advantage. The PCs will need to pick a side (or else figure out a way to ride out the coming storm).<br /> <br /> The recent fall from grace of a local ancilla has put their domain up for grabs and the Prince has decided to award it to the young PC Coterie to manage for the next year on a probationary basis. If they do well, they'll get it formally, increasing their Status and raising their rank among the city's Kindred. If they fail, they're unlikely to get another chance for advancement for decades and will be hapless fodder for ruthless Harpies. Complicating matters is a rival Coterie who wanted the domain, as well as certain allies of the former holder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T10:30:38-07:00","id":1495439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1495385-episode-and-story-ideas-for-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1495416#post1495416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have homebrewed a system to use backgrounds in a more meaningful/strategical way. My chronicle is more traditional, but one of the Characters is a powerful arms industry tycoon and he can engage in economical warfare against his rivals. Apart for that, all Backgrounds have an in-game use, as they have to be &quot;tapped&quot; to get info, special equipment or favours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just out of curiosity, how did you get around the snowball mechanic where the Backgrounds produced more Backgrounds at an almost exponential rate?<br /> <br /> Part of the reason I suggested this for a shorter game was the fact it implodes with enough time due to power creep. I messed around with the notion of making regional Background stats rather than standalone character Backgrounds, but that created a lot of book keeping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T11:25:48-07:00","id":1495446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1495385-episode-and-story-ideas-for-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1495439#post1495439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just out of curiosity, how did you get around the snowball mechanic where the Backgrounds produced more Backgrounds at an almost exponential rate?<br /> <br /> Part of the reason I suggested this for a shorter game was the fact it implodes with enough time due to power creep. I messed around with the notion of making regional Background stats rather than standalone character Backgrounds, but that created a lot of book keeping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two ways..The first is that I force the characters to use their backgrounds a lot for necessary tasks: want incendiary ammo for a raid? Tap 1 Resources. Want to have an audience with an Elder? Tap1 Status. Want info on a street gang? Tap 1 contact. The chronicle is quite intense, as the Coterie is the first line of defence against a potential Sabbat siege, so they usually spend half their backgrounds on that. <br /> The second one is conflict. The players can attack or be attacked by NPC's, which requires a massive use of background and can lead to loss of dots. A PC lost contacts and later an ally against a Sabbat pack. The Coterie has made some powerful enemies even in the local Camarilla now, so if they get too powerful some strong Elders will start attacking them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T13:54:52-07:00","id":1495492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1495385-episode-and-story-ideas-for-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1495446#post1495446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two ways..The first is that I force the characters to use their backgrounds a lot for necessary tasks: want incendiary ammo for a raid? Tap 1 Resources. Want to have an audience with an Elder? Tap1 Status. Want info on a street gang? Tap 1 contact. The chronicle is quite intense, as the Coterie is the first line of defence against a potential Sabbat siege, so they usually spend half their backgrounds on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the idea that conflict during a story can reduce or outright delete Backgrounds, but what do you mean by tapping?<br /> <br /> The entire Background system revolves around the notion of simplification rather than simulation, so any use of a lower rank doesn't reduce the overall score. Did you run the Backgrounds like a point buy system where you would buy results and then have to work to refill the score?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T20:41:32-07:00","id":1495510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1495385-episode-and-story-ideas-for-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1495492#post1495492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the idea that conflict during a story can reduce or outright delete Backgrounds, but what do you mean by tapping?<br /> <br /> The entire Background system revolves around the notion of simplification rather than simulation, so any use of a lower rank doesn't reduce the overall score. Did you run the Backgrounds like a point buy system where you would buy results and then have to work to refill the score?</div> </div> </div> </div>To start with, my game is a bit different to what most people play. We do a play by post with a reduced number of player (3+ ST) in an environment that has sandbox elements but also an overarching story. Strategy and simulation play an important role, as the PC's are tasked with stopping the first stages of a Sabbat siege (it looks a little like ep3 of the Ventrue Chronicle, even though I didn't know about it when I started the game). <br /> We use a weekly system (in-game, not IRL), and during a week players can &quot;tap&quot; their backgrounds to get perks, info, access to NPC's... Or use them to increase their background even further. Every new week the Backgrounds are &quot;refreshed&quot; and can be used again.<br /> It's a fairly simulationist system, which I wouldn't probably use in a face to face or even video hosted game. But it works pretty well in text based and it helps define really well the difference between the type of backgrounds and their numerical value. Because in a &quot;normal&quot; game, what's the real difference between contacts 3 and 4? Influence 2 or 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}